Confirmed and conclusive: Meta permanently removed the Facebook Groups API (including `groups_access_member_info` and group feed read access) on April 22, 2024, and this has cascaded to shutdowns of Groups integrations across Zapier, Make, Zoho, Sprinklr, and others. There is no sanctioned API path left to retrieve group post content for a third-party client. The only remaining route is scraping, which Meta's Automated Data Collection Terms explicitly prohibit. This is a clear T2 failure: the core function depends on a single third party (Meta) whose access has already been revoked, and the alternative (scraping) is not permitted by platform terms.

